    "result_text": "The build passes and all tests are green. Let me verify the whole thing compiled cleanly (MapStruct mapper generated the nested identity) \u2014 the successful test proves the endpoint returns the v2 shape. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased **version 2 of the owner identity**, keeping structural impact low by adding one small helper class and making tiny, cohesive edits to each identifier derivation rather than growing any function.\n\n**V2 region tag inside identifiers** \u2014 New `IdentityRegion.code(owner)` returns `\"V2\" + Locality.region(owner)`. The three identifier derivations now consume it:\n- `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 memberId leading segment (`NSW\u2026` \u2192 `V2NSW\u2026`)\n- `AssignHouseholdId` \u2014 mixed into the hashed key\n- `CheckUniqueIdentity.identityKey` \u2014 mixed into the hashed raw string\n\nBecause every V2 value carries the `V2` prefix (memberId literally; the hash inputs cryptographically), **no value produced under v1 recurs**, and duplicate/household detection stays internally consistent since both sides hash identically.\n\n**Locality stays plain** \u2014 `Locality`, `Timezone`, and `OwnerSegment` still call `Locality.region/locality` directly, so `locality` remains `\"NSW\"`, and the segment's area (`STANDARD_METRO`) has no V2 tag. The audit output confirms: `memberId=V2NSW2716E6609E7` but `ownerSegment:\"STANDARD_METRO\"`.\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 In `openapi.yml`, added an `OwnerIdentity` schema (memberId/householdId/identityKey), referenced it as a nested `identity` object, added top-level integer `apiVersion`, and removed the three now-nested top-level fields. `OwnerMapper` gained a small `identity(owner)` builder plus `apiVersion` = 2 mappings; the three old top-level mappings were removed.\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreatedEvent` moved to schema v2: added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the (v2) owner DTO.\n\nFiles touched: `openapi.yml`, `OwnerMapper`, `AuditOwnerCreatedEvent`, `AssignCustomerCode`, `AssignHouseholdId`, `CheckUniqueIdentity`, plus the new `IdentityRegion`. Test result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
