    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the answer.\n\n## `POST /api/owners` \u2014 ordered pipeline\n\nDefined by `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Everything below runs inside a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the end. The whole endpoint is first gated by security.\n\n**0. Authorization gate** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is denied (403) before any step runs.\n\nThen, in order:\n\n| # | Step (class) | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **CheckIdempotencyKey** | Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it. *Validation/short-circuit:* if the key was already used, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 replays the original owner as **200** and creates nothing. |\n| 2 | **BuildOwner** | Reads and validates the `@RequestBody`. Records `sharesHousehold`. Requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (composed from `addressLine1/2` or normalized from `address`), `city`, `telephone` \u2014 any missing/blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**). Normalizes telephone to **E.164** (invalid length \u2192 400 on `telephone`). Sets normalized address/address lines. Validates email format if present (bad \u2192 400 on `email`). `registrationDate` defaults to today via the mapper if absent. Publishes the built `Owner`. |\n| 3 | **CheckEmailDomain** | *Validation:* rejects a disposable-provider email domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 400 on `email`. Absent email is skipped. |\n| 4 | **ValidatePostcode** | *Validation:* if a postcode is present, must be 4 digits and within the city's fixed region range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 else 400 on `postcode`. Absent postcode skipped. |\n| 5 | **AssignHouseholdId** | *Side-effect:* sets a deterministic `householdId` = SHA-256 hash of region + normalized lastName + postcode. |\n| 6 | **CheckUniqueIdentity** | *Validation:* computes an `identityKey` (SHA-256 over region + normalized telephone + lower email + Soundex(lastName)); if any non-deleted existing owner has the same full key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**). This is the sole hard duplicate gate. |\n| 7 | **CheckCityCapacity** | *Validation:* if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**). |\n| 8 | **FlagCapacityWarning** | *Side-effect:* sets `capacityWarning = true` when the city holds 40\u201349 owners (excludes this one). |\n| 9 | **AdjustRegistrationDate** | *Validation:* a future `registrationDate` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). *Side-effect:* rolls the date forward off weekends and fixed 2026 holidays to the next business day. |\n| 10 | **CheckDailyLimit** | *Validation:* if \u2265 100 owners already registered for that (adjusted) date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**). |\n| 11 | **AssignCustomerCode** | *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode`/memberId = `<REGION><FY2><HASH8><LuhnCheckDigit>`. |\n| 12 | **DeduplicateCustomerCode** | *Side-effect:* if that code collides with an existing owner, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to make it unique. |\n| 13 | **AssignNamesakeCount** | *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive). |\n| 14 | **FlagBulkSignup** | *Side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners already registered that date. |\n| 15 | **FlagPossibleDuplicate** | *Side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicateOf` = id of an existing owner with same postcode and phonetically-equal (Soundex) lastName but a different identityKey. Skipped when postcode absent or `sharesHousehold = true`. |\n| 16 | **SaveOwner** | *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id). |\n| 17 | **RecordIdempotencyKey** | *Side-effect:* if a key was supplied, stores the new owner DTO under it for future replay. |\n| 18 | **AuditOwnerCreated** | *Side-effect:* logs an `AUDIT` line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel). |\n| 19 | **AuditOwnerCreatedEvent** | *Side-effect:* logs a structured `OWNER_CREATED` `AUDIT` event with a monotonic `seq`, id, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment. |\n| 20 | **NotifyWelcome** | *Side-effect:* logs a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger (enqueues welcome notification). |\n| 21 | **RespondWithOwnerCreated** | *Side-effect:* responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/<id>` and the owner DTO body. |\n\n### Summary\n\n**Validations (in the order they can reject), and their status codes:**\n1. Role `OWNER_ADMIN` (403)\n2. Idempotency replay short-circuit (200, not a rejection)\n3. Required fields present + telephone E.164 + email format (400)\n4. Email domain not disposable (400)\n5. Postcode format/region (400)\n6. Identity uniqueness (409)\n7. City capacity < 50 (409)\n8. Registration date not in the future (400)\n9. Daily limit < 100 (429)\n\n**Side-effects (in order):** assign householdId \u2192 flag capacityWarning \u2192 adjust registrationDate \u2192 assign customerCode \u2192 dedupe customerCode \u2192 set namesakeCount \u2192 flag bulkSignupWarning \u2192 flag possibleDuplicateOf \u2192 **persist owner** \u2192 record idempotency key \u2192 audit log \u2192 audit event log \u2192 welcome notification log \u2192 201 response with Location header.\n\nOne note: the YAML comment at `assignHousehold` says members are \"capped by MembershipLevel,\" but no step in the current pipeline enforces such a cap \u2014 `MembershipLevel` is only computed at DTO-mapping time, not used as a gate here."
